Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?perf=20phase=2011=20patch=200114=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?fix=20slot=200112=20PRELOAD=5FMIDI=20per-track=20PPQ=20regressi?=
 =?UTF-8?q?on?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (Phase 11 iter I correctness fix). Slot 0112 introduced an
in-memory MIDI event cache so song changes wouldn't re-parse from CF;
that path shipped a latent timing bug.

Symptom (operator iter H PLAY1, 2026-05-07):
  "title music is only playing a single note every 5 seconds, they
  are different notes, so like playing the MIDI but extremely slow"

Root cause: load_from_preload_cache copied events into _events but
left _division_ppq at whatever the LAST preload call set. The WiiWare
set is NON-uniform -- white.mid is 24 PPQ while the other 40 tracks
are 480 PPQ -- so after the 41-track preload loop _division_ppq was
24, and any cache hit for a 480-PPQ track got _us_per_tick =
500000/24 = 20833 (~20x too slow) instead of the correct
500000/480 = 1041.

Engine log evidence (iter H OPL3.LOG):
  parsed wanpaku.mid = 8241 events at 480 PPQ
  parsed anzen.mid   = 1731 events at 480 PPQ
  ... 38 more 480-PPQ tracks ...
  parsed white.mid   = 7284 events at 24 PPQ
  preload complete - 41 tracks cached, 0 failed
  load_from_preload_cache: hit 'curly' = 5684 events  <- played at 24 PPQ rate

Fix: store _division_ppq in the cache entry alongside events.
load_from_preload_cache restores both before start() runs.

Memory cost delta: +2 bytes per entry x 41 entries = +82 bytes total.

Bonus: cache-hit log now reports per-entry PPQ for self-diagnosis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 src/sound/MidiScheduler.h   | 19 +++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
index 8da53df..41512f8 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp
@@ -138,9 +138,16 @@ bool MidiScheduler::add_to_preload_cache(const std::string &path,
   // Capture the parsed event list (whether ok or not -- empty events
   // for parse failures still get cached so we know not to retry on
   // the same key).
+  // patch 0114: also capture _division_ppq into the cache entry. The
+  // WiiWare set is non-uniform (white.mid = 24 PPQ; rest = 480 PPQ),
+  // so the global _division_ppq is unreliable at play-time after
+  // multi-track preload. Storing per-entry preserves correct timing.
   if (ok)
   {
-    _preload_cache[cache_key] = std::move(_events);
+    PreloadCacheEntry entry;
+    entry.events       = std::move(_events);
+    entry.division_ppq = _division_ppq;
+    _preload_cache[cache_key] = std::move(entry);
   }
 
   // Restore prior _events (currently empty unless a track was somehow
@@ -170,24 +177,25 @@ bool MidiScheduler::load_from_preload_cache(const std::string &cache_key)
   // Copy from cache. ~5000 events x 12 bytes = ~60 KB; fast (sub-ms
   // memcpy) vs 446 ms file-parse spike. The cache retains its own
   // copy so subsequent loads of the same track don't re-parse.
-  _events = it->second;
+  _events = it->second.events;
+
+  // patch 0114: restore the cached _division_ppq for THIS track.
+  // Without this, the global _division_ppq retained whatever the
+  // last-preloaded track set -- for the WiiWare set, white.mid is
+  // 24 PPQ while the other 40 tracks are 480 PPQ, giving a 20x tempo
+  // skew on cache hits for any non-matching track (iter H operator-
+  // perceived "1/10 speed" symptom). start() will _recompute_us_per_-
+  // tick using this restored division + the SMF-default tempo it
+  // resets to.
+  _division_ppq = it->second.division_ppq;
 
   // Reset playback position (same as load() does on parse success).
   _next_event_idx = 0;
   _current_tick = 0;
   _position_us = 0;
 
-  // _division_ppq is preserved across cache hits because it's set by
-  // _parse_smf at preload time AND not reset by start(). For multiple
-  // tracks with different divisions, the most-recently-cached track's
-  // division wins -- Cave Story tracks all use either 480 PPQ
-  // (WiiWare) or 24 PPQ (ORGMID) within the same source dir; first
-  // track preloaded establishes the active division for the run.
-  // (Robust fix would cache division per-key; deferred to wave-N+1
-  // if real-HW W26-A iter shows mistuned playback for some tracks.)
-
-  LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler::load_from_preload_cache: hit '{}' = {} events",
-           cache_key, (unsigned)_events.size());
+  LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler::load_from_preload_cache: hit '{}' = {} events at {} PPQ",
+           cache_key, (unsigned)_events.size(), (unsigned)_division_ppq);
   return true;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.h b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.h
index aac6479..558666d 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiScheduler.h
+++ b/src/sound/MidiScheduler.h
@@ -240,12 +240,19 @@ private:
   std::unique_ptr<MidiBackend> _backend;
 
   // patch 0112 (Phase 11 iter H opt #1: front-load MIDI parsing).
-  // In-memory cache of pre-parsed event lists, keyed by track name
-  // (e.g., "curly", "white", "gravity"). Populated at init via
-  // add_to_preload_cache; consulted at play-time via
-  // load_from_preload_cache. Empty by default (env unset -> no
-  // preload). Resident size ~2 MB max (41 tracks x ~50 KB each).
-  std::unordered_map<std::string, std::vector<MidiEvent>> _preload_cache;
+  // patch 0114 (Phase 11 iter I fix): cache stores _division_ppq per
+  // entry. The WiiWare set is non-uniform -- `white.mid` is 24 PPQ
+  // while the other 40 tracks are 480 PPQ. Without per-entry storage,
+  // load_from_preload_cache leaves _division_ppq at whatever the
+  // last-preloaded track set, mistuning playback by 20x for any
+  // track that doesn't match. (iter H operator-perceived "1/10
+  // speed" symptom on title music after preload of all 41 tracks.)
+  struct PreloadCacheEntry
+  {
+    std::vector<MidiEvent> events;
+    std::uint16_t          division_ppq;
+  };
+  std::unordered_map<std::string, PreloadCacheEntry> _preload_cache;
   std::uint16_t _division_ppq          = 480;  // SMF default if header had 0
   std::uint32_t _tempo_us_per_quarter  = 500000;  // SMF default = 120 BPM
   double        _us_per_tick           = 500000.0 / 480.0;
